<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile sells antimony metal and ore.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile sells antimony metal and ore.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center said it sold 610,109 lbs of antimony for $549,978 to Amalgamated Corp, Aaron Ferer, and Ney Smelting and Refining.</p>
<p>In addition, Stockpile sold 512,742 lbs of antimony sulfide ore, containing approximately 333,282 lbs of antimony, for approximately $45,300.</p>
<p>The next receipt of offers for antimony is June 24.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
